{"diagnosis": "Loopback divider 64 send 0xa5 never produced a received byte, giving TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received and FAIL 0xdead instead of a received 0xa5. Expected reg_dat_we to load {1'b1, data, 1'b0} with 10 bits when idle, but TX stayed in dummy idle with send_pattern ~0 and send_bitcnt reloading 15. Root cause is line 123 in picosoc/simpleuart.v where send_dummy <=1 keeps the send_dummy && !send_bitcnt branch dominant and starves the reg_dat_we branch. CONE_SLICE only offers picosoc/spiflash.v:52 and scripts/quartus/system.v:57 with no simpleuart cover, so trace wins.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@
			if (send_dummy && !send_bitcnt) begin
				send_pattern <= ~0;
				send_bitcnt <= 15;
				send_divcnt <= 0;
-				send_dummy <= 1;
+				send_dummy <= 0;
			end else
			if (reg_dat_we && !send_bitcnt) begin
", "expected": "tohost PASS, uart loopback 0xa5 received with no timeout"}

